+Built on **FHIR R4**. The filing core is rule-based and designed to fail safe rather than guess. An **optional NLP layer** (`app/nlp.py`, needs `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`) lets people use plain language; the model only interprets text, deterministic code makes every decision, and nothing is auto-confirmed.
 
 ## What it does
 
@@ -27,12 +27,25 @@ Built on **FHIR R4**. It is rule-based (no machine learning), and it is designed
 4. **Observation normalizer** (`app/normalize.py`): converts units (HbA1c mmol/mol to %, glucose
    mmol/L to mg/dL) and flags implausible values for human review instead of "fixing" them.
 
+## Natural-language layer (optional)
+
+Set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (and optionally `NLP_MODEL`). Without it these endpoints return 503 and everything else works.
+
+| Endpoint | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| `POST /ask` `{"text": "show records for Jane Doe"}` | Plain language in, source-linked records out. The model reads only the request, never the chart. Two matching names return candidates, never a guess. `/ask-page` is a small page with a microphone button. |
+| `POST /nlp/suggest-code` `{"text": "sugar disease"}` | Free text to ranked ICD-10 candidates. Also used as a fallback when filing a free-text Condition; result is flagged `needs-coding-review`. |
+| `POST /nlp/extract-note` `{"note": "...", "patient_id": "p1"}` | Note to draft findings (negations like "no diabetes" kept apart) and **unconfirmed** Condition drafts. Nothing is written to the chart. |
+
+Limits: a spoken name is not authentication (add real login before any pilot); model output is validated but
+not clinically evaluated; sending text to a model API needs a BAA/DPA and de-identification for real data.
+
